Z||000002||Jay||09-17-2001||01:57 PM||||Welcome Blondie88.  First off where are you located and what year style fiero does he have?  What is he really wanting for his car? <P>I've had great success dealing with Race Tech  in Toronto, better known as the Fiero shop.  They can be reached at 416-747-5728 (www.thefieroshop.com)  They have everything from instrument white out gauges to engine conversions and everything in between.  With the exchange rate as it is it may be worth looking at them.<P>Of course there is also Pisa, V8 archie, and others on this board who have shops and stores that specialize in the Fiero.  I can only speak for the ones I deal with but most if not all are reputable.  Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Blondie88||09-17-2001||02:21 PM||||Thank you so very much for all your help.  No one seems to want to take my money though.  I would very easily just give my boyfriend a note saying i'm giving him 400 dollars, but he'd rip it up and probably kill me. So i'm a little dramatic....but yeah, i'm going to keep trying and hopefully it'll work.  <P>I'm from North Dakota by the way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Sorry I didn't include that in my profile.  My boyfriend has an 86 GT.  Thank you for trying to help me again!||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroFanaticus2||09-17-2001||02:44 PM||||Are his windows tinted?  I sell a precut window tint kit for $29.99 plus $5.20 shipping that would give him something to do with his car that would be an inexpensive 'stocking stuffer'.  I only have 8 kits left for this season though and only forum members get that price.  You could also try searching ebay for 'Fiero', that'll give you some more ideas. <A HREF="http://crowd.to/fierotint" TARGET=_blank>http://crowd.to/fierotint</A>  is the tint website||||reg||1
